pack aurekai-rubicon-programs
generation control-1
provenance the Rubicon pass, 2026-08-27 -- stop improving local systems, start forcing them to collapse into shared machinery
authority measured
note Fifteen shared-machine programs, each recorded at the rung it has actually earned. Fourteen are at 'defined', which is rung 0. Nothing here claims to be built. What IS measured is the evidence that the factoring is warranted: twelve duplicate mechanic families with file:line citations, and a Partner Commons that is now loaded, latent-addressable and benchmarked rather than described.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT MOVED FROM PROSE TO STATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

upgrade upg:partner-commons-loaded
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  claim The 112 Partner Commons profiles now exist as state, not as a document.
  before partner_commons.py had existed the whole time with record_profile and record_observation; the ONLY PartnerProfile anywhere in the estate was a Run8 test fixture
  after 112 profiles across 35 families in ~/.bonfyre/partner-commons.sqlite3, loaded through the existing API with no new schema
  fidelity parsed count is exactly 112, matching the map's own claim; zero duplicate ids
  preservation the source table's 'provides' and 'family' columns have no schema field, so they are recorded as declared PartnerObservations rather than dropped
  note this is the difference between having a standard library and having a document about one

upgrade upg:partner-commons-latent-addressable
  status LANDED
  verification MEASURED
  claim Partner Commons method retrieval is now a measured capability.
  pipeline partner_commons -> bonfyre-embed --backend onnx (nomic-embed-text-v1.5 int8, 768d) -> bonfyre-vec (sqlite-vec SIMD) -> semantic_derivation
  prerequisite this only became possible today; bonfyre-embed --backend onnx was silently falling back to hashed tokens until the model directory was laid out
  measurement_held_out connects_to shared with a latent neighbour: 92.0% (103/112) against a 50.9% random draw, +41.1 pts. connects_to is never embedded.
  note the geometry recovers declared organ attachment from specialty text alone

claim clm:hook-retrieval-benchmarked
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  claim Latent retrieval recovers the map's own deep-promotion hook assignments far above chance.
  answer_key the map's "Primary-path deep-promotion coverage by hook" section is a human-authored labelled dataset; 18 usable hooks, 191 partner assignments
  discipline queries are hook DESCRIPTIONS written without naming any partner; the answer key never reaches the retriever
  result recall@10 49.6%, precision@10 25.9%, random recall@10 2.6%, lift +47.0 pts
  strong finance P@10 100%, risk R@10 100%, routing R@10 55%, time R@10 100%
  weak compiler, context, surface score 0 -- their gold entries are largely outside the 112
  correction a first pass reported 45.6% using a tolerant name matcher; substring matching let "Git" swallow "GitHub discovery" and "QUIC" swallow "QuickFIX", corrupting the gold set. Exact matching only, and misses are reported rather than absorbed.

claim clm:partner-commons-coverage-gap
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  claim The 112-profile index does not cover the methods the map's own hook table depends on.
  evidence 94 of 191 answer-key assignments (49%) name methods absent from the 112
  evidence 44 distinct missing methods, including BitNet, CUE, YaFF, Restate, Feldera/DBSP, BLAKE3, Apache Arrow, Tree-sitter, simdjson, Zstd, OpenSSL, Vectorscan, ONNX Runtime, llama.cpp/GGUF, ggml, Cloudflare, Harbor, Hugging Face, Automerge, Iroh, OpenDAL
  evidence one hook, federation, has NO reachable gold at all
  cause the map itself names five profile groups "outside the 112 Partner index" -- late_assimilation, operational_agent, extended_operational, financial_specialty, quantitative_risk
  consequence recall@10 is measured over REACHABLE gold only; scoring against unreachable answers would understate the retriever for a corpus reason
  action the Partner Commons index needs those 44 methods before Program I can route the whole hook surface

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DENSITY EVIDENCE -- why the factoring is warranted (Program O)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim clm:twelve-duplicate-mechanic-families
  status STANDING
  verification MEASURED
  method independent audit of the 85 control-plane modules, read-only, file:line evidence required
  claim Twelve duplicate mechanic families exist in the control plane today.
  family_01 sqlite schema+ensure_schema+CRUD triple, 21 modules
  family_02 money/value/cost stores independently implemented in economic_graphs, financial_metabolism, food_combination_engine, household_economic_circuit
  family_03 cooling/reheat/backoff state machines outside scheduling.py -- proof_frontier, target_obligation, resource_metabolism, provider_state
  family_04 candidate scoring/ranking outside route_ranker -- provider_graphs:74, bonfyre_sid:89, evidence_binding:83
  family_05 vector embedding/similarity outside latent_fabric -- bonfyre_sid:35-93 reimplements projection, Hamming ordering
  family_06 YaFF block parsing implemented twice -- pack_loader:56-87 and opportunity:304-366 parse the same grammar
  family_07 form field/evidence-slot specs -- atomic_forms Field/EvidenceSlot vs form_graph FieldSpec/EvidenceSpec
  family_08 canonical JSON + SHA-256 identity, 5 modules
  family_09 the same sqlite_master existence probe locally defined in 9 modules
  family_10 ISO-8601 UTC serialization, 13 modules, identical astimezone/replace/isoformat
  family_11 ISO-8601 parsing with naive-to-UTC normalization, 5 near-identical helpers
  family_12 timestamped subject-state observation records -- provider_state.Observation vs partner_commons.PartnerObservation
  consequence families 9, 10 and 11 are pure mechanical duplication and could be factored with no semantic risk; families 2, 4 and 5 are the ones that matter, because they are the Allocation and Ranking fabrics already existing in triplicate

claim clm:organs-exist-but-are-unbound
  status STANDING
  verification VERIFIED_ON_DISK
  claim The fabrics are not missing. They exist as separate organs that were never bound to each other.
  evidence opportunity.py carries Opportunity/Blocker/Unlock and reachability, with NO value dimension
  evidence economic_graphs.py carries money, value, cost and commitment, with NO opportunity binding
  evidence scheduling.py already implements StandingSet -> Effect: Watch, schedule, record_check, reheat, due, frontier_subjects
  evidence route_ranker, capability_closure, financial_metabolism, latent_fabric, foreign, address_plane all exist and are individually sound
  consequence the Rubicon is not a build program, it is a binding program; the user's diagnosis is confirmed in code

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE 15 PROGRAMS -- all at rung 0 except where noted
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

note Thirteen of the fifteen are recorded in capability_catalog at 'defined' (rung 0). Two -- F-observation-fabric and I-partner-marketplace -- are at 'implemented' (rung 1), because real code ran against real state for those and only those. Naming a program is not building it, and the catalog must not be readable as if it were.

program A-opportunity-fabric
  maturity defined
  factors AI Leads, Fleming, Personal, Zcrawl, Partner Commons, Model Commons, Upper90, Ventures, Aurekai, Run8
  existing_organ opportunity.py (reachability half), economic_graphs.py (value half)
  gap the two halves are not bound; Opportunity has no potential_value, probability, option_value, expiry or information_value
  partner_methods Hummingbot, Interledger, OpenGamma Strata, NautilusTrader

program B-allocation-fabric
  maturity defined
  factors AI Loss fee splits, JRSS ownership, Upper90 cost allocation, Fleming capital, Personal budget, model compute, WorkGraph obligations
  existing_organ financial_metabolism.py with its basis law
  law list/contracted/estimated/accrued/billed/authorized/captured/settled/paid/accounting/allocated/credit never silently collapse
  partner_methods Formance, Interledger, Hummingbot, Fyle
  note the strongest single candidate; family_02 shows it already exists three times

program C-standing-effect-runtime
  maturity defined
  factors JRSS statements, AI Loss reconciliation, Upper90 remediation, Personal watches, Fleming deadlines, Run8 continuation
  existing_organ scheduling.py -- Watch/schedule/record_check/reheat/due already IS this machine
  gap five other modules implement cooling/backoff independently (family_03)
  partner_methods Temporal, Kill Bill, Restate, celld

program D-ranking-fabric
  maturity defined
  catalog_rung 0 -- 'partial' is not a catalog maturity; prior work exists but the FABRIC is unbuilt
  factors partner selection, model selection, provider routing, deals, offers, Zcrawl frontier, work prioritization
  existing_organ route_ranker.TernaryRanker
  measured_today the AI Leads cascade is real: 45.1% ternary -> 49.1% real-valued + selective SSM, oracle 83.0%
  measured_today ternary quantization costs 2.3 pts aggregate and the cost is widening
  gap three other modules rank independently (family_04)
  partner_methods vectorbt, QuantConnect LEAN, ArcticDB, Weights & Biases

program E-physical-cell-fabric
  maturity defined
  gap NO partner method in the 112 covers geography; the latent route returns finance profiles because there is nothing closer
  action needs new profiles before it can be routed at all

